  "title": "Creamy Zucchini Soup",
  "description": "If you like Maggi broth cubes, add one to the soup while it is being boiled. By doing so, it is no longer needed to add salt, pepper, or herbs.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This deliciuos Creamy Zucchini Soup is extremely easy to cook. Only three main ingredients: zucchinis, onions and milk.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21299,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1710054133205} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21299-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Creamy Zucchini Soup</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_0349.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tIf you like Maggi broth cubes, add one to the soup while it is being boiled. By doing so, it is no longer needed to add salt, pepper, or herbs.\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>5 zucchinis</li><li>3 onions</li><li>3 cloves of garlic</li><li>3-4 Tbsp olive oil</li><li>salt and ground pepper</li><li>300 ml water</li><li>300 ml milk (2%)</li><li>100 ml heavy cream</li><li>1 tsp mix of herbs de Provence</li><li>Few pinches of paprika (for serving)</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Peel and chop onions.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_0320.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Peel and chop garlic.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_0322.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Cut the zucchinis.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_0327.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>In a large pot, heat the olive oil, add onions and garlic. Cook until golden, while stirring constantly.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_0321.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Add zucchinis, and sauté for about 5 minutes. Add salt and pepper.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_0329.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Add water, milk and heavy cream. The level of liquid should just cover the veggies. Bring to a boil. Reduce the heat, add  the herbs of Provence and simmer about 20 minutes. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_0331.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Puree the soup with blender until smooth. If the soup is too thick, add some milk or heavy cream. Bring to a boil once again and remove the pan from the heat. Taste the soup, and add salt and pepper accordingly.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_0333.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Serve the creamy soup and don't forget to sprinkle with paprika or decorate with fresh herbs.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_0348-2.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Soup</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
